{"title":"TorontoAI + AWS User Group - Demo Day ","startsAt":"2026-11-04T17:00:00-05:00","endsAt":"2026-11-04T19:00:00-05:00","status":"ACTIVE","type":"PHYSICAL","description":"Ask Your Data Warehouse Questions With a Model You Host Yourself\nShort abstract (for the agenda):\n\nA live demo of db-agent, an open-source text-to-SQL agent, querying a Databricks warehouse using a local LLM through Ollama. No model API, no per-question token bill, nothing leaving your network. I'll also show the guardrail that stops the agent from running a destructive query.\nLonger version (if they ask for one):\n\nText-to-SQL is everywhere now. Running it on a metered model API means every question has a price, and many teams can't send schema to an outside model at all. In this demo I'll run db-agent with a local model through Ollama against a Databricks SQL warehouse on AWS. You'll see what a self-hosted model handles well, where it fails, and the read-only safety layer that keeps it from changing data. Code is open source: github.com/db-agent/db-agent","venue":{"name":"Amazon Toronto Office (YYZ16)","address":"40 King St W, Toronto, ON M5H 3Y2, Canada, Toronto","lat":43.649496,"lng":-79.37953,"city":"Toronto"},"fee":null,"group":"Toronto AI Meetup","image":"https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/7/1/6/b/highres_531389035.jpeg"}